IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc-definitions`

-- ccc17-warrants.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 487.092 to 488: warrants for prints and impressions, the duty of the person executing
-- certain warrants, applications by telecommunication, search without a warrant in exigent circumstances, the publication ban, orders denying access to information, and the
-- execution of a search warrant by day. Layer 1: the law, objectively. Same conventions as ccc17-dna-orders.l4. `s 2 day` and `s 2 night` (ccc-definitions) are called directly;
-- the other section 2 answers are seam inputs.

§ `Section 487.092 -- Information for impression warrant`

-- covers: 487.092(1), 487.092(1)(a), 487.092(1)(b)
-- fork: F1
-- jural: a justice > the person whose print or impression is to be obtained > power
-- src:9759 | 487.092 (1) A justice may issue a warrant in writing authorizing a peace officer to do any thing, or cause any thing to be done under the direction of the peace officer, described in the warrant in order to obtain any handprint, fingerprint, footprint, foot impression, teeth impression or other print or impression of the body or any part of the body in respect of a person if the justice is satisfied
-- src:9760 | (a) by information on oath in writing that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been committed and that information concerning the offence will be obtained by the print or impression; and
-- src:9761 | (b) that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to issue the warrant.
@ref s 487.092(1) (src:9759-9761)
GIVEN `the justice is satisfied by information on oath in writing that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been committed and that information concerning the offence will be obtained by the print or impression` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice is satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to issue the warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.092(1) the justice may issue a warrant in writing authorizing a peace officer to obtain a print or impression of the body of the person` MEANS
    IF `the justice is satisfied by information on oath in writing that there are reasonable grounds to believe that an offence against this or any other Act of Parliament has been committed and that information concerning the offence will be obtained by the print or impression` AND `the justice is satisfied that it is in the best interests of the administration of justice to issue the warrant`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 487.092(2)
-- jural: the person whose print or impression is to be obtained > a justice > right
-- src:9763 | (2) A warrant issued under subsection (1) shall contain such terms and conditions as the justice considers advisable to ensure that any search or seizure authorized by the warrant is reasonable in the circumstances.
@ref s 487.092(2) (src:9763)
GIVEN `the justice considers the term or condition advisable to ensure that any search or seizure authorized by the warrant is reasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.092(2) the warrant shall contain the term or condition` MEANS
    IF `the justice considers the term or condition advisable to ensure that any search or seizure authorized by the warrant is reasonable in the circumstances`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 487.092(3)
-- fork: F14
-- jural: a peace officer > the person named in the warrant > power
-- src:9765 | (3) A warrant issued under subsection (1) may be executed at any place in Canada. Any peace officer who executes the warrant must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed.
@ref s 487.092(3) (src:9765)
GIVEN `the place of execution is in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the peace officer has authority to act as a peace officer in the place where the warrant is executed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.092(3) the warrant may be executed by the peace officer at the place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the place of execution is in Canada` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the peace officer has authority to act as a peace officer in the place where the warrant is executed` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must have authority to act as a peace officer in the place where it is executed"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 487.093 -- Duty of person executing certain warrants`

-- covers: 487.093(1)
-- jural: none
-- src:9770 | 487.093 (1) A person who executes a warrant issued under subsection 110.1(5), 117.0101(6), 117.04(1), 199(1), 395(1) or 487(1) shall, during that execution,
@ref s 487.093(1) (the warrants named) (src:9770)
-- The warrants named: subsections 110.1(5), 117.0101(6), 117.04(1), 199(1), 395(1) and 487(1). A list not closed with "only": another warrant is NOTHING.
`s 487.093(1) the warrants` MEANS LIST
    (`Provision of the Code` OF 110.1, "(5)")
    (`Provision of the Code` OF 117.0101, "(6)")
    (`Provision of the Code` OF 117.04, "(1)")
    (`Provision of the Code` OF 199, "(1)")
    (`Provision of the Code` OF 395, "(1)")
    (`Provision of the Code` OF 487, "(1)")

DECLARE `s 487.093(1) what the person executing the warrant shall do` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.093(1)(a) give a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1 to the person present and ostensibly in control of the building, receptacle or place to be searched`
    `s 487.093(1)(b) affix the copy and the notice in a prominent location within the building or place or on or next to the receptacle`
    `s 487.093(1)(c) give the copy and the notice to the person to be searched`
    `s 487.093(2) subsection (1) does not apply because the warrant authorizes the search of a thing detained after it was lawfully seized`

-- covers: 487.093(1), 487.093(1)(a), 487.093(1)(b), 487.093(1)(c), 487.093(2)
-- jural: the person searched, or in control of the place searched > the person who executes the warrant > right
-- src:9770 | 487.093 (1) A person who executes a warrant issued under subsection 110.1(5), 117.0101(6), 117.04(1), 199(1), 395(1) or 487(1) shall, during that execution,
-- src:9771 | (a) give the following to any person who is present and ostensibly in control of the building, receptacle or place to be searched:
-- src:9772 | (i) a copy of the warrant, and
-- src:9773 | (ii) a notice in Form 5.1 setting out the address of the court before which anything seized during the execution may be brought or from which a copy of a report on anything so seized may be obtained;
-- src:9774 | (b) affix the copy and the notice in a prominent location within the building or place or on or next to the receptacle, if there is no person present and ostensibly in control of the building, receptacle or place; or
-- src:9775 | (c) give the copy and the notice to the person to be searched, if the warrant is issued under subsection 395(1) for the search of a person.
-- src:9776 | Exception
-- src:9777 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the warrant authorizes the search of anything that is detained under this Act after it has been lawfully seized.
@ref s 487.093(1) and (2) (what to do) (src:9770-9777)
GIVEN `the provision under which the warrant is issued` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `a person is present and ostensibly in control of the building, receptacle or place to be searched` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant is issued under subsection 395(1) for the search of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant authorizes the search of anything that is detained under this Act after it has been lawfully seized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 487.093(1) what the person executing the warrant shall do`
`s 487.093(1) what the person executing the warrant shall do during the execution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (elem `the provision under which the warrant is issued` `s 487.093(1) the warrants`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the warrant authorizes the search of anything that is detained under this Act after it has been lawfully seized` THEN JUST `s 487.093(2) subsection (1) does not apply because the warrant authorizes the search of a thing detained after it was lawfully seized`
        IF `the warrant is issued under subsection 395(1) for the search of a person` THEN JUST `s 487.093(1)(c) give the copy and the notice to the person to be searched`
        IF `a person is present and ostensibly in control of the building, receptacle or place to be searched` THEN JUST `s 487.093(1)(a) give a copy of the warrant and a notice in Form 5.1 to the person present and ostensibly in control of the building, receptacle or place to be searched`
        OTHERWISE JUST `s 487.093(1)(b) affix the copy and the notice in a prominent location within the building or place or on or next to the receptacle`

@ref s 487.093(2) (the exception) (src:9777)
GIVEN `the warrant authorizes the search of anything that is detained under this Act after it has been lawfully seized` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.093(2) subsection (1) does not apply` MEANS
    IF `the warrant authorizes the search of anything that is detained under this Act after it has been lawfully seized`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply if the warrant authorizes the search of anything that is detained under this Act after it has been lawfully seized."

§ `Section 487.1 -- Warrants, etc., by telecommunication`

DECLARE `s 487.1(1) applicant` IS ONE OF
