-- covers: 487.1(1)(o)
-- jural: none
-- src:9797 | (o) an order under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018;
@ref s 487.1(1)(o) (src:9797)
GIVEN `the section number of the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 487.1(1)(o) the order is under one of sections 487.013 to 487.018` MEANS
    `the section number of the order` AT LEAST 487.013 AND `the section number of the order` AT MOST 487.018

-- covers: 487.1(1)
-- fork: F1
-- jural: the Attorney General, a peace officer or a public officer > the judge or justice > power
-- src:9779 | 487.1 (1) Despite anything in this Act, the Attorney General, a peace officer or a public officer may, if they are permitted to apply for any of the following, submit their application by a means of telecommunication:
@ref s 487.1(1) (src:9779)
-- "may, if they are permitted to apply for any of the following, submit their application by a means of telecommunication": a grant whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING.
-- Paragraph (m): a warrant under subsection 487.01(1) only if it does not authorize the observation of a person by means of a television camera or other similar electronic device.
GIVEN applicant IS A `s 487.1(1) applicant`
      `the applicant is permitted to apply for the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision under which the instrument is sought` IS A `Provision of the Code`
      `the warrant under subsection 487.01(1) authorizes the observation of a person by means of a television camera or other similar electronic device` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.1(1) the application may be submitted by a means of telecommunication` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF applicant EQUALS `s 487.1(1) someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the applicant is permitted to apply for the instrument` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the provision under which the instrument is sought` EQUALS (`Provision of the Code` OF 487.01, "(1)") AND `the warrant under subsection 487.01(1) authorizes the observation of a person by means of a television camera or other similar electronic device` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF elem `the provision under which the instrument is sought` `s 487.1(1) the provisions` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 487.1(1)(o) the order is under one of sections 487.013 to 487.018` (`the provision under which the instrument is sought`'s `section`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed)

-- covers: 487.1(2)
-- jural: a person who must swear an oath > the court > privilege
-- src:9810 | (2) A person who must swear an oath in connection with an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing may, instead of swearing the oath, make a statement in writing stating that all matters submitted in support of the application are true to their knowledge and belief, and the statement is deemed to be a statement made under oath.
@ref s 487.1(2) (src:9810)
GIVEN `the person must swear an oath in connection with an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person makes a statement in writing stating that all matters submitted in support of the application are true to their knowledge and belief` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.1(2) the statement is deemed to be a statement made under oath` MEANS
    IF `the person must swear an oath in connection with an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` AND `the person makes a statement in writing stating that all matters submitted in support of the application are true to their knowledge and belief`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 487.1(3)
-- jural: the applicant > a judicial officer > right
-- src:9812 | (3) A judicial officer who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing shall certify the application as to time and date of receipt.
@ref s 487.1(3) (src:9812)
GIVEN `the person is a judicial officer who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.1(3) the judicial officer shall certify the application as to time and date of receipt` MEANS
    IF `the person is a judicial officer who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 487.1(4)
-- jural: the applicant > a judicial officer > disability
-- src:9814 | (4) An application under subsection 487.01(5.2) shall not be submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing.
@ref s 487.1(4) (src:9814)
GIVEN `the application is under subsection 487.01(5.2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.1(4) the application shall not be submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` MEANS
    IF `the application is under subsection 487.01(5.2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 487.1(5)
-- jural: the applicant > a judicial officer > privilege
-- src:9816 | (5) An applicant may submit their application by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing only if it would be impracticable in the circumstances to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing.
@ref s 487.1(5) (src:9816)
GIVEN `it would be impracticable in the circumstances to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.1(5) the applicant may submit the application by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` MEANS
    IF `it would be impracticable in the circumstances to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An applicant may submit their application by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing only if it would be impracticable in the circumstances"

-- covers: 487.1(6)
-- jural: a judicial officer > the applicant > right
-- src:9818 | (6) An application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing shall include a statement of the circumstances that make it impracticable to submit the application by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing.
@ref s 487.1(6) (src:9818)
GIVEN `the application is submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application includes a statement of the circumstances that make it impracticable to submit it by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.1(6) the application includes the statement of circumstances the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the application includes a statement of the circumstances that make it impracticable to submit it by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall include a statement of the circumstances that make it impracticable"

-- covers: 487.1(7)
-- jural: a judicial officer > the applicant > power
-- src:9820 | (7) Any oath required in connection with an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing may be administered by a means of telecommunication.
@ref s 487.1(7) (src:9820)
GIVEN `an oath is required in connection with an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.1(7) the oath may be administered by a means of telecommunication` MEANS
    IF `an oath is required in connection with an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 487.1(8)
-- jural: the applicant > a judicial officer > right
-- src:9822 | (8) A judicial officer who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing shall record the application verbatim, in writing or otherwise, and certify the record or a transcription of it as to time, date and contents.
@ref s 487.1(8) (src:9822)
GIVEN `the person is a judicial officer who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.1(8) the judicial officer shall record the application verbatim and certify the record or a transcription of it as to time, date and contents` MEANS
    IF `the person is a judicial officer who receives an application submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- covers: 487.1(9)
-- jural: the person subject to the warrant > a judicial officer > immunity
-- src:9824 | (9) If an application is submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing, the judicial officer shall not issue the warrant, order, extension or authorization unless he or she is satisfied that the application discloses reasonable grounds for dispensing with its submission by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing.
@ref s 487.1(9) (src:9824)
-- A bar: the judicial officer shall not issue ... "unless" satisfied. JUST TRUE = the bar applies (not satisfied); JUST FALSE = the "unless" is met.
GIVEN `the application is submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judicial officer is satisfied that the application discloses reasonable grounds for dispensing with its submission by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.1(9) the judicial officer is barred from issuing the warrant, order, extension or authorization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is submitted by a means of telecommunication that does not produce a writing` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the judicial officer is satisfied that the application discloses reasonable grounds for dispensing with its submission by a means of telecommunication that produces a writing` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall not issue the warrant, order, extension or authorization unless he or she is satisfied that the application discloses reasonable grounds for dispensing with its submission"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 487.1(10) step` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.1(10)(a) the judicial officer completes and signs the document, noting on its face the time and date`
    `s 487.1(10)(b) the judicial officer transmits a copy of the document to the applicant by that means`
    `s 487.1(10)(c) the applicant transcribes the document, as directed by the judicial officer, noting on its face the name of the judicial officer as well as the time and date`

-- covers: 487.1(10), 487.1(10)(a), 487.1(10)(b), 487.1(10)(c)
-- jural: the applicant > a judicial officer > power
-- src:9826 | (10) A judicial officer who issues the warrant, order, extension or authorization may do so by a means of telecommunication, in which case
-- src:9827 | (a) the judicial officer shall complete and sign the document in question, noting on its face the time and date;
-- src:9828 | (b) if the means of telecommunication produces a writing, the judicial officer shall transmit a copy of the document to the applicant by that means; and
-- src:9829 | (c) if the means of telecommunication does not produce a writing, the applicant shall, as directed by the judicial officer, transcribe the document, noting on its face the name of the judicial officer as well as the time and date.
@ref s 487.1(10) (src:9826-9829)
GIVEN `the judicial officer issues the warrant, order, extension or authorization by a means of telecommunication` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the means of telecommunication produces a writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF `s 487.1(10) step`)
`s 487.1(10) the steps that follow when the judicial officer issues the document by a means of telecommunication` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judicial officer issues the warrant, order, extension or authorization by a means of telecommunication` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the means of telecommunication produces a writing` THEN JUST (LIST `s 487.1(10)(a) the judicial officer completes and signs the document, noting on its face the time and date`, `s 487.1(10)(b) the judicial officer transmits a copy of the document to the applicant by that means`)
        OTHERWISE JUST (LIST `s 487.1(10)(a) the judicial officer completes and signs the document, noting on its face the time and date`, `s 487.1(10)(c) the applicant transcribes the document, as directed by the judicial officer, noting on its face the name of the judicial officer as well as the time and date`)

-- covers: 487.1(11), 487.1(11) "judicial officer"
-- jural: none
-- src:9831 | (11) The following definitions apply in this section.
-- src:9832 | judicial officer means a judge or justice who is authorized, under the applicable provision of this Act, to issue a warrant, order, extension or authorization referred to in subsection (1). (fonctionnaire judiciaire)
@ref s 487.1(11) "judicial officer" (src:9831-9832)
GIVEN `the person is a judge or justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is authorized, under the applicable provision of this Act, to issue a warrant, order, extension or authorization referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.1(11) judicial officer` MEANS
    IF `the person is a judge or justice` AND `the person is authorized, under the applicable provision of this Act, to issue a warrant, order, extension or authorization referred to in subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "judicial officer means a judge or justice who is authorized, under the applicable provision of this Act, to issue a warrant, order, extension or authorization referred to in subsection (1)"

-- covers: 487.1(11) "public officer"
-- jural: none
-- src:9833 | public officer means a public officer who is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament. (fonctionnaire public)
@ref s 487.1(11) "public officer" (src:9833)
GIVEN `the person is a public officer who is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the duties of the person include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.1(11) public officer` MEANS
    IF `the person is a public officer who is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law` AND `the duties of the person include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "public officer means a public officer who is appointed or designated to administer or enforce a federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this Act or any other Act of Parliament"

§ `Section 487.11 -- Where warrant not necessary`

-- covers: 487.11
-- fork: F1
-- jural: a peace officer or a public officer > the person searched or whose place is searched > power
-- src:9835 | 487.11 A peace officer, or a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce any federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament, may, in the course of his or her duties, exercise any of the powers described in subsection 487(1) or 492.1(1) without a warrant if the conditions for obtaining a warrant exist but by reason of exigent circumstances it would be impracticable to obtain a warrant.
@ref s 487.11 (src:9835)
-- "may ... exercise any of the powers described in subsection 487(1) or 492.1(1) without a warrant if the conditions for obtaining a warrant exist but by reason of exigent circumstances it would be
-- impracticable to obtain a warrant": a grant whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (fork F1). Peace officer: the answer of section 2 "peace officer", taken as an input.
GIVEN `s 2 peace officer: the person is one` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce any federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts in the course of their duties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions for obtaining a warrant exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `by reason of exigent circumstances it would be impracticable to obtain a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.11 the officer may exercise the powers described in subsection 487(1) or 492.1(1) without a warrant` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 2 peace officer: the person is one` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the person is a public officer who has been appointed or designated to administer or enforce any federal or provincial law and whose duties include the enforcement of this or any other Act of Parliament`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the person acts in the course of their duties` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the conditions for obtaining a warrant exist` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `by reason of exigent circumstances it would be impracticable to obtain a warrant` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 487.2 -- Restriction on publication`

-- covers: 487.2, 487.2(a), 487.2(b), 487.2 closing words
-- jural: the person occupying or suspected in relation to the place searched > any person who publishes > right
-- src:9837 | 487.2 If a search warrant is issued under section 487 or a search is made under such a warrant, everyone who publishes in any document, or broadcasts or transmits in any way, any information with respect to
-- src:9838 | (a) the location of the place searched or to be searched, or
-- src:9839 | (b) the identity of any person who is or appears to occupy or be in possession or control of that place or who is suspected of being involved in any offence in relation to which the warrant was issued,
-- src:9840 | without the consent of every person referred to in paragraph (b) is, unless a charge has been laid in respect of any offence in relation to which the warrant was issued, guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction.
@ref s 487.2 (src:9837-9840)
-- "everyone who publishes ... without the consent of every person referred to in paragraph (b) is, unless a charge has been laid ..., guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction".
-- "without the consent" limits the offence in its own wording (NOTHING outside it); "unless a charge has been laid" is the text's own no (JUST FALSE).
GIVEN `a search warrant is issued under section 487 or a search is made under such a warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person publishes in any document, or broadcasts or transmits in any way, the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is about the location of the place searched or to be searched` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is about the identity of a person who is or appears to occupy or be in possession or control of that place or who is suspected of being involved in any offence in relation to which the warrant was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `every person referred to in paragraph (b) consents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a charge has been laid in respect of any offence in relation to which the warrant was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.2 the person is guilty of an offence punishable on summary conviction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`a search warrant is issued under section 487 or a search is made under such a warrant` AND `the person publishes in any document, or broadcasts or transmits in any way, the information`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT (`the information is about the location of the place searched or to be searched` OR `the information is about the identity of a person who is or appears to occupy or be in possession or control of that place or who is suspected of being involved in any offence in relation to which the warrant was issued`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `every person referred to in paragraph (b) consents` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `a charge has been laid in respect of any offence in relation to which the warrant was issued` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a charge has been laid in respect of any offence in relation to which the warrant was issued"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 487.2 (the punishment) (src:9837-9840)
`s 487.2 the punishments` MEANS LIST
    Punishment OF `on summary conviction`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

§ `Section 487.3 -- Order denying access to information`

DECLARE `s 487.3(1) who makes the order` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.3(1) a justice`
    `s 487.3(1) a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction`
    `s 487.3(1) a judge of the Court of Quebec`
    `s 487.3(1) someone else`

-- covers: 487.3(1), 487.3(1)(a), 487.3(1)(b)
-- fork: F1
-- jural: a justice or a judge > any person who seeks the information > power
-- src:9842 | 487.3 (1) On application made at the time an application is made for a warrant under this or any other Act of Parliament, an order under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 or an authorization under section 529 or 529.4, or at a later time, a justice, a judge of a superior court of criminal jurisdiction or a judge of the Court of Quebec may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, any information relating to the warrant, order or authorization on the ground that
-- src:9843 | (a) the ends of justice would be subverted by the disclosure for one of the reasons referred to in subsection (2) or the information might be used for an improper purpose; and
-- src:9844 | (b) the reason referred to in paragraph (a) outweighs in importance the access to the information.
@ref s 487.3(1) (src:9842-9844)
GIVEN `who makes the order` IS A `s 487.3(1) who makes the order`
      `the application is made at the time an application is made for a warrant under this or any other Act of Parliament, an order under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 or an authorization under section 529 or 529.4, or at a later time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ends of justice would be subverted by the disclosure for one of the reasons referred to in subsection (2), or the information might be used for an improper purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that reason outweighs in importance the access to the information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.3(1) the justice or judge may make an order prohibiting access to, and the disclosure of, any information relating to the warrant, order or authorization` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `who makes the order` EQUALS `s 487.3(1) someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the application is made at the time an application is made for a warrant under this or any other Act of Parliament, an order under any of sections 487.013 to 487.018 or an authorization under section 529 or 529.4, or at a later time` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `the ends of justice would be subverted by the disclosure for one of the reasons referred to in subsection (2), or the information might be used for an improper purpose` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF NOT `that reason outweighs in importance the access to the information` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 487.3(2) reason` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.3(2)(a)(i) disclosure of the information would compromise the identity of a confidential informant`
    `s 487.3(2)(a)(ii) disclosure of the information would compromise the nature and extent of an ongoing investigation`
    `s 487.3(2)(a)(iii) disclosure of the information would endanger a person engaged in particular intelligence-gathering techniques and thereby prejudice future investigations in which similar techniques would be used`
    `s 487.3(2)(a)(iii.1) disclosure of the information would be injurious to international relations, national defence or national security`
    `s 487.3(2)(a)(iv) disclosure of the information would prejudice the interests of an innocent person`
    `s 487.3(2)(b) any other sufficient reason`

-- covers: 487.3(2), 487.3(2)(a), 487.3(2)(b)
-- jural: none
-- src:9846 | (2) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(a), an order may be made under subsection (1) on the ground that the ends of justice would be subverted by the disclosure
-- src:9847 | (a) if disclosure of the information would
-- src:9848 | (i) compromise the identity of a confidential informant,
-- src:9849 | (ii) compromise the nature and extent of an ongoing investigation,
-- src:9850 | (iii) endanger a person engaged in particular intelligence-gathering techniques and thereby prejudice future investigations in which similar techniques would be used,
-- src:9851 | (iii.1) be injurious to international relations, national defence or national security, or
-- src:9852 | (iv) prejudice the interests of an innocent person; and
-- src:9853 | (b) for any other sufficient reason.
@ref s 487.3(2) (src:9846-9853)
GIVEN reason IS A `s 487.3(2) reason`
      `the other reason is sufficient` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.3(2) the ground is one on which an order under subsection (1) may be made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF reason EQUALS `s 487.3(2)(b) any other sufficient reason` AND NOT `the other reason is sufficient` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- covers: 487.3(3)
-- jural: any person who seeks the information > the justice or judge > disability
-- src:9855 | (3) Where an order is made under subsection (1), all documents relating to the application shall, subject to any terms and conditions that the justice or judge considers desirable in the circumstances, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, any term or condition concerning the duration of the prohibition, partial disclosure of a document, deletion of any information or the occurrence of a condition, be placed in a packet and sealed by the justice or judge immediately on determination of the application, and that packet shall be kept in the custody of the court in a place to which the public has no access or in any other place that the justice or judge may authorize and shall not be dealt with except in accordance with the terms and conditions specified in the order or as varied under subsection (4).
@ref s 487.3(3) (src:9855)
GIVEN `an order is made under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.3(3) all documents relating to the application shall be placed in a packet, sealed and kept in the custody of the court` MEANS
    IF `an order is made under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an order is made under subsection (1)"

DECLARE `s 487.3(4) judge to whom the application is made` IS ONE OF
    `s 487.3(4) the justice or judge who made the order`
    `s 487.3(4) a judge of the court before which any proceedings arising out of the investigation in relation to which the warrant or production order was obtained may be held`
    `s 487.3(4) someone else`

-- covers: 487.3(4)
-- fork: F6
-- jural: a person who applies to terminate or vary the order > the justice or judge > power
-- src:9857 | (4) An application to terminate the order or vary any of its terms and conditions may be made to the justice or judge who made the order or a judge of the court before which any proceedings arising out of the investigation in relation to which the warrant or production order was obtained may be held.
@ref s 487.3(4) (src:9857)
-- The subsection names the judges to whom an application to terminate or vary may be made but not who may apply (fork F6): the function answers the forum only.
GIVEN `the judge to whom the application is made` IS A `s 487.3(4) judge to whom the application is made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 487.3(4) the application to terminate the order or vary its terms and conditions may be made to the judge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the judge to whom the application is made`
    WHEN `s 487.3(4) someone else` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 488 -- Execution of search warrant`

-- covers: 488, 488(a), 488(b), 488(c)
-- jural: the person whose place is searched > a peace officer > right
-- src:9859 | 488 A warrant issued under section 487 shall be executed by day, unless
-- src:9860 | (a) the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for it to be executed by night;
-- src:9861 | (b) the reasonable grounds are included in the information; and
-- src:9862 | (c) the warrant authorizes that it be executed by night.
@ref s 488 (src:9859-9862)
-- "A warrant issued under section 487 shall be executed by day, unless (a) ...; (b) ...; and (c) ...": the three limbs are cumulative.
GIVEN `the warrant was issued under section 487` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for it to be executed by night` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasonable grounds are included in the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant authorizes that it be executed by night` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488 the warrant shall be executed by day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the warrant was issued under section 487` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)
        IF `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for it to be executed by night` AND `the reasonable grounds are included in the information` AND `the warrant authorizes that it be executed by night` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be executed by day, unless (a) the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for it to be executed by night; (b) the reasonable grounds are included in the information; and (c) the warrant authorizes that it be executed by night"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The same rule at a time of day, using section 2 "day" and "night" (ccc-definitions): minutes after midnight (6:00 is 360, 21:00 is 1260). At exactly 6:00 or 21:00 section 2 says nothing (NOTHING).
@ref s 488 (at a time of day) (src:9859-9862)
GIVEN `the time of day the warrant is executed, in minutes after midnight` IS A NUMBER
      `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for it to be executed by night` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reasonable grounds are included in the information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the warrant authorizes that it be executed by night` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 488 the warrant may be executed at the time of day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2 day` `the time of day the warrant is executed, in minutes after midnight` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2 night` `the time of day the warrant is executed, in minutes after midnight` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for it to be executed by night` AND `the reasonable grounds are included in the information` AND `the warrant authorizes that it be executed by night` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 2 night` `the time of day the warrant is executed, in minutes after midnight` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be executed by day, unless (a) the justice is satisfied that there are reasonable grounds for it to be executed by night"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent)
